[{:db/id "q-38631/selection/32b694e7aa131f284f729b2a3bea18c700b6de430843ac8a635c28a0600a96aa" :answer/id #uuid "c60975ab-4b18-54c2-8e2c-3940ec530f8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{II}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38631/selection/4e115bbc2c9d29ab867431cd42932d3e10325670ede34bd4fc551a9cd345ded3" :answer/id #uuid "e72d541f-aec8-5a7f-9d98-0f666890228f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{I}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38631/selection/ad7ef8fa013fdf0f7b84cbf81b59897b959a2004d69c890fb8ad20ca441dad75" :answer/id #uuid "d2bcba5f-f15a-59a3-8100-485375f52eb9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the given graphs are correct" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38631/selection/500f30cea6a2bee526d42ef19673a5fa97cea6e08aabf77dedb47066f370551a" :answer/id #uuid "5bfe35e4-00c2-5464-b07f-99d56aa47deb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{III}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38631/selection/7c28bd84f9100fb35e61829bf6eff99c723771d1cd360349d8d2cfe6796c5bb2" :answer/id #uuid "c002fa28-3671-509d-925c-a0fcdbec6529" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{IV}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38631/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "066039b4-c4ea-5b0c-9153-3a330e70231a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-38631/selection/4e115bbc2c9d29ab867431cd42932d3e10325670ede34bd4fc551a9cd345ded3" :answer-field/choices ["q-38631/selection/32b694e7aa131f284f729b2a3bea18c700b6de430843ac8a635c28a0600a96aa" "q-38631/selection/4e115bbc2c9d29ab867431cd42932d3e10325670ede34bd4fc551a9cd345ded3" "q-38631/selection/ad7ef8fa013fdf0f7b84cbf81b59897b959a2004d69c890fb8ad20ca441dad75" "q-38631/selection/500f30cea6a2bee526d42ef19673a5fa97cea6e08aabf77dedb47066f370551a" "q-38631/selection/7c28bd84f9100fb35e61829bf6eff99c723771d1cd360349d8d2cfe6796c5bb2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-38631" :question/id #uuid "c24c4df2-fb09-5691-82c4-3a6a2dad1c5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-38631" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13941629/assets/f801d9b46aa43cb1065c2935513aee7cc0e448378423735c05ec6df7da89ff8d.png)\n\nWhich of the above could be the graph of $y=(x+2)(x+1)^{2}(x-1)?$" :question/worked-solution "Based on the factored equation, we can make the following conclusions about the graph:\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the roots $x=-2,1$ is $1,$ which is odd, the graph must cross the $x$-axis at this point. Moreover, because $x=-2,1$ are simple roots, the graph must *not* be tangent to the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the root $x=-1$ is $2,$ which is even, the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at this point.\n\nOnly the graphs $\\text{I}$ and $\\text{III}$ satisfy these conditions.\n\nTo choose between these two graphs, we need to consider the end behavior. Since the leading coefficient is positive, as $x$ approaches $\\infty ,$ $y$ approaches $\\infty .$\n\nOnly graph $\\text{I}$ displays this end behavior. Therefore, the correct answer is $\\text{I}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-38631/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d03ac24f-82a6-5af8-b1b8-9021e521d47a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38631"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-38779/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "7ca19fa0-327a-5758-a43f-13ca69c44585" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38779/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "007758cc-2581-53fb-85f8-c171e4eff159" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38779/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "23c0a00e-4526-5472-865c-33dc5a708088" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38779/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "23b4e068-b4e2-5bbe-894e-92eb6b7279be" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38779/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "abadd53d-36c3-5af6-99bb-1b102fa335d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38779/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "769829b0-61dc-5684-84c1-01f194ad19f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-38779/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-38779/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-38779/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-38779/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-38779/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-38779/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-38779" :question/id #uuid "0953767a-d6e0-5ca3-b7a7-3f6ef5307bd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-38779" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13941629/assets/737052513985954a32dcce369fce60f898474db846319ca31b36e3e4682b4b37.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $x=-4$ is a root of odd multiplicity.\n- $p(0)=3.$\n- $x=1$ is a root of odd multiplicity." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The root $x=-4$ has an even multiplicity because at $x=-4$ the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction.\n\n- Statement II is true. The graph passes through the $y$-axis at $y=3$, which means that $p(0)=3.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The root $x=1$ has an odd multiplicity because the graph passes through the $x$-axis at the point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-38779/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38779"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80352/selection/b6cdf7e5d909b0489c30c725ef1dbd69b6338eee653f028c4e999dd2d342f60a" :answer/id #uuid "0ba0aa0e-6296-559b-a9b0-b74d701046c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-x(x+2)^{7}(x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80352/selection/e2a1c131e3b66d5fc19dc24fec55d4360d8fa36e7a2a0326af95a1cace7ce687" :answer/id #uuid "a1ede83d-33ba-57d7-a9bf-fce67f091cee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-x(x+2)^{5}(x-1)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80352/selection/4cecf2e7bcfd7fbe5b077f701293113b6bde65d73bd9490cf42eb7772c155673" :answer/id #uuid "7792575a-cd70-544d-896c-5470726b0532" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-{x}^{2}(x+2)(x-1)^{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80352/selection/fe8eb27d18d43627a42165330890139ab759c2b41252f5e477a5461732622185" :answer/id #uuid "14826cf4-67b7-5f0a-86a1-b6e41c50982a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-{x}^{3}(x+2)^{5}(x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80352/selection/7977bde90441699ff7fb97cbe30071317efcf09ced02ff793323abf519f81adb" :answer/id #uuid "c520863c-23e7-568f-b35c-b76b57f8ebfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-x(x+2)^{3}(x-1)^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80352/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "299f4e81-2632-5fb2-8a69-a67a10ca4269" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80352/selection/7977bde90441699ff7fb97cbe30071317efcf09ced02ff793323abf519f81adb" :answer-field/choices ["q-80352/selection/b6cdf7e5d909b0489c30c725ef1dbd69b6338eee653f028c4e999dd2d342f60a" "q-80352/selection/e2a1c131e3b66d5fc19dc24fec55d4360d8fa36e7a2a0326af95a1cace7ce687" "q-80352/selection/4cecf2e7bcfd7fbe5b077f701293113b6bde65d73bd9490cf42eb7772c155673" "q-80352/selection/fe8eb27d18d43627a42165330890139ab759c2b41252f5e477a5461732622185" "q-80352/selection/7977bde90441699ff7fb97cbe30071317efcf09ced02ff793323abf519f81adb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80352" :question/id #uuid "f48448f1-4b70-5bcf-83fd-82afeaf27fb8" :question/math-academy-id "q-80352" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13941629/assets/1956e8c684cc03538877d3ec5d1e72d3d3f48b63341f7739b9a18962b080f1e3.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the equation of the polynomial curve shown above?" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice that the function has precisely three distinct roots, $x=-2,x=0$ and $x=1.$\n\nBased on the graph, we can make the following conclusions about the multiplicities of the roots:\n\n- Since the graph passes through $x=-2,$ this root has odd multiplicity, and since the graph is tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=-2,$ the multiplicity must be greater than one.\n\n- Since the graph is *not* tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=0,$ this root is a simple root (the multiplicity equals $1$).\n\n- Since the graph passes through $x=1,$ this root has odd multiplicity, and since the graph is tangent to the $x$-axis at $x=1,$ the multiplicity must be greater than one.\n\nFrom the given options, the only possible equation is $y=-x(x+2)^{3}(x-1)^{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80352/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fc09a0f-34d3-5ca9-9964-6cb00498bfa7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80352"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-112587/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "a73de4b7-7530-505e-89c1-de84f0a24286" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112587/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "06d4903e-0219-5d80-919a-28340f77d80f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112587/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" :answer/id #uuid "36d748d3-ba59-5c5a-b61c-d2f482c1137d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112587/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "f3b0c2a7-a3b8-537e-b8cb-c8c9c74fc968" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112587/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "42fc4c0c-155d-5430-8adf-68d6ecf34fa3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112587/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b739cd9a-c4b5-57e3-b50c-6e39b6caef2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-112587/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-112587/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-112587/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-112587/selection/c5361bc7e0ee1fc99d41021ab98e1ca699e408307178f1c31af6bc0071e78ea0" "q-112587/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-112587/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-112587" :question/id #uuid "e2a037df-404e-52d9-92f6-f45ec38b1c2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-112587" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13941629/assets/aa431232a1f9ef2374f4e8a9c0202cf60ce1dcfef69c2a6fca604fe6aed7b681.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $p(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty .$\n- $p(0)=0.$\n- $x=1$ is a root of even multiplicity." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. As $x$ moves left in the negative direction towards $-\\infty ,$ the $y$ value moves down in the negative direction towards $-\\infty .$\n\n- Statement II is true. The graph passes through the $y$-axis at $y=0$, which means that $p(0)=0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The root $x=1$ has an odd multiplicity because the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-112587/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112587"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-112599/selection/4e115bbc2c9d29ab867431cd42932d3e10325670ede34bd4fc551a9cd345ded3" :answer/id #uuid "c084bf6e-084e-5644-9745-dd6f1dc747e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{I}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112599/selection/ad7ef8fa013fdf0f7b84cbf81b59897b959a2004d69c890fb8ad20ca441dad75" :answer/id #uuid "5647c201-e248-5ed9-9f82-c35b11da1a49" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the given graphs are correct" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112599/selection/500f30cea6a2bee526d42ef19673a5fa97cea6e08aabf77dedb47066f370551a" :answer/id #uuid "ad5ca4a1-aae1-5e90-840f-2681f819a431" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{III}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112599/selection/32b694e7aa131f284f729b2a3bea18c700b6de430843ac8a635c28a0600a96aa" :answer/id #uuid "7aaf244d-f2b0-591f-897a-52065342a0be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{II}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112599/selection/7c28bd84f9100fb35e61829bf6eff99c723771d1cd360349d8d2cfe6796c5bb2" :answer/id #uuid "0714e920-5c19-53f0-a8df-9b7bf53cd659" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{IV}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112599/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "15d33e1f-9e7a-53d0-9138-93ebb23cfe48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-112599/selection/4e115bbc2c9d29ab867431cd42932d3e10325670ede34bd4fc551a9cd345ded3" :answer-field/choices ["q-112599/selection/4e115bbc2c9d29ab867431cd42932d3e10325670ede34bd4fc551a9cd345ded3" "q-112599/selection/ad7ef8fa013fdf0f7b84cbf81b59897b959a2004d69c890fb8ad20ca441dad75" "q-112599/selection/500f30cea6a2bee526d42ef19673a5fa97cea6e08aabf77dedb47066f370551a" "q-112599/selection/32b694e7aa131f284f729b2a3bea18c700b6de430843ac8a635c28a0600a96aa" "q-112599/selection/7c28bd84f9100fb35e61829bf6eff99c723771d1cd360349d8d2cfe6796c5bb2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-112599" :question/id #uuid "4c02154d-80d7-5924-a668-7afcb107c078" :question/math-academy-id "q-112599" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13941629/assets/1586e286d2b07aac28a42f91c76318ae209c46c19e14e429c62f0770ada9393b.png)\n\nWhich of the above could be the graph of $y=-x(x+2)^{2}(x-2)^{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "Based on the factored equation, we can make the following conclusions about the graph:\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the root $x=-2$ is $2,$ which is even, the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at this point.\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the root $x=0$ is $1,$ which is odd, the graph must cross the $x$-axis at this point. Moreover, because $x=0$ is a simple root, the graph must *not* be tangent to the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the root $x=2$ is $3,$ which is odd, the graph must cross the $x$-axis at this point. Moreover, because $x=2$ is a triple-root, the graph must be tangent to the $x$-axis at this point.\n\nOnly the graphs $\\text{I}$ and $\\text{IV}$ satisfy these conditions.\n\nTo choose between these two graphs, we need to consider the end behavior. Since the leading coefficient is negative, as $x$ approaches $\\infty ,$ $y$ approaches $-\\infty .$ Since only graph $\\text{I}$ displays this end behavior, the correct answer is $\\text{I}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-112599/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d03ac24f-82a6-5af8-b1b8-9021e521d47a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112599"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
